# ---------------- Veterans ----------------
@kind ambient
@topic veteran
@who *
@needs veteran
templates are a second job
anyone else spend more time on their template than playing?
str capped, dex two points short, story of my life
plan your realm abilities before you hit 50, trust me
purge first, then think about the rest
my first character took months, alts go so much faster
i remember when nobody knew where anything was
the people make this game, not the loot
seen a lot of guilds come and go
first time i saw a dragon i just stood there and died
if a stealther hits you, dont run in a straight line
best advice i ever got: always know where the zone line is
spent more on gems this month than on my house
leveling an alt is easy when you know every camp
every class feels weak until you learn it
i still remember my first real group, we wiped all night
used to think 20 was high level
spec deep, dont spread your points, learned that the hard way
the frontier is where the real game is
lost count of my deaths in the frontier years ago
a good healer is worth ten good drops
my old guild did the dragon every friday, good times
learned more from wiping than from winning
speed is everything once you leave the keep
back when i started, buffbots were just a rumor
an 8 man that knows each other beats a zerg every time
the trick to leveling is good company, the xp follows
still have my first sword, cant bring myself to sell it
nothing beats the first time you take a keep
miss being new sometimes, everything was a surprise
